<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Acme AI contribution memo, {{ month }}</title>
<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 42rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #1b1b1b; background: #fff; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .25rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; }
  td.n, th.n { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #eee; background: #111; } th, td { border-color: #444; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Acme AI contribution memo, {{ month }}</h1>

<h2>What this memo measures</h2>
<p>Contribution profit is revenue, net of credits and discounts, less inference cost, cloud cost
(direct plus allocated shared) and support cost. Support is part of cost of revenue. This is the
project's own definition, not any company's.</p>
<p>This is the walking-skeleton memo. It reports revenue only: the cost components, the allocation
rules and the flags are not built yet, so no profit or margin is shown.</p>
<p>All figures are synthetic. The books belong to a generated company, "Acme AI".</p>

<h2>Headline</h2>
<p>Total revenue for {{ month }}: <strong>{{ ('rollup/' ~ month ~ '/revenue') | num }}</strong>.</p>

<h2>Revenue by account</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Name</th><th class="n">Revenue</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for a in accounts %}
<tr><td>{{ a.account_id }}</td><td>{{ a.display_name }}</td><td class="n">{{ ('cp/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ a.account_id ~ '/revenue') | num }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>Tie-out to the general ledger</h2>
<p>Account revenue less the ledger, by revenue code. Every difference must be zero for the month to close.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>GL code</th><th class="n">Difference</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for code in gl_codes %}
<tr><td>{{ code }}</td><td class="n">{{ ('pnl/' ~ month ~ '/' ~ code) | num }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>Where each number comes from</h2>
<p>Every figure above carries its number ID. <code>margin explain &lt;number-id&gt;</code> prints the
chain from the figure down to the hashed source rows.</p>
</body>
</html>
